WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.025
As a diagram grows, finding a task means searching a
larger chart and more source.

00:00:06.145 --> 00:00:10.170
Diagram outline puts the elements in one searchable list.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.690
This example uses a small delivery plan.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.910
You can navigate without changing the source.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.180
Start with the View tab.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.375
Open Outline from View, or find it through Commands.

00:00:26.495 --> 00:00:30.770
The list shows the diagram elements with their types and
source lines.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.440
Type Design in the search field to narrow the list.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.060
The matching entry stays easy to identify.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.505
Searching itself leaves the plan unchanged.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.758
You can also keep the outline docked beside the diagram.

00:00:48.878 --> 00:00:52.628
Open it, search for Design, then choose Dock outline.

00:00:52.748 --> 00:00:57.723
Select the Design task from the filtered list to navigate
to that element.

00:00:57.843 --> 00:01:02.018
The outline stays useful while you work through a larger
document.

00:01:02.138 --> 00:01:05.913
One searchable view connects the diagram to its source.
